# LeakSanitizer suppressions for muyo-llm.
#
# Consumed via LSAN_OPTIONS (not ASAN_OPTIONS: the `leak:` syntax is LeakSanitizer's, and
# AddressSanitizer rejects it) — see scripts/sanity.sh sanitize.

# pthread_once initialization frame (glibc)
leak:^__pthread_once_slow$
leak:nptl/pthread_once.c

# AMDVLK driver teardown. It leaks a small fixed amount when the instance and device are
# destroyed. It is the driver, not this program, and AMDVLK is the only driver on the
# development machine that exposes VK_KHR_cooperative_matrix (docs/Findings.md), so it is
# the one that has to run there.
leak:amdvlk64.so

# The Vulkan loader dlopen()s the ICD from a library constructor and never unloads it, so
# its allocations outlive main() by design. The stack is `<unknown module>` <- call_init <-
# _dl_init; matching call_init suppresses it without hiding a leak in this program.
leak:call_init
leak:_dl_init
